q('raft-election','short_answer','Distributed systems','Explain how Raft elects a leader and reduces split votes.',[],['randomized|random','majority|quorum','term'],'Candidates increment their term and request votes. A majority elects a leader; randomized election timeouts reduce repeated split votes.','raft','hard',criteria=['randomized|random','majority|quorum','term'],rubric='Award exactly one point for each of the following five independently expressed facts. Do not infer unstated facts: 1. A follower starts an election after its election timeout. 2. The candidate increases its term. 3. The candidate votes for itself and requests votes. 4. A majority of votes elects the leader. 5. Randomized election timeouts reduce repeated split votes.')
