q('mutex-homework','homework','Operating systems','Explain how a mutex can prevent a lost update to a shared counter.',[],['mutual exclusion|one thread','critical section|lock','read|update'],'Protect the entire read-modify-write operation with the same mutex. Mutual exclusion prevents threads from interleaving the critical section.','ostep',criteria=['mutual exclusion|one thread','critical section|lock','read|update'],rubric='Award exactly one point for each of the following five independently expressed facts. Do not infer unstated facts: 1. All writers use the same mutex. 2. Acquire the mutex before reading the counter. 3. Keep the read-modify-write operation inside the critical section. 4. Release the mutex after writing. 5. Mutual exclusion prevents concurrent execution of the protected operation.',dueAt='2026-12-31T23:59:59Z')
q('retry-collaborative','collaborative','Distributed systems','Work together: how can a service avoid applying a retried request twice?',[],['identifier|idempotency|serial','store|cache|record','duplicate|retry'],'Give each request a stable identifier, record its result, and return that result when the same request is retried.','raft',criteria=['identifier|idempotency|serial','store|cache|record','duplicate|retry'],rubric='Award exactly one point for each of the following five independently expressed facts. Do not infer unstated facts: 1. Use a stable unique request identifier. 2. Store the result associated with that identifier. 3. Detect repeated identifiers. 4. Return the stored result for a duplicate. 5. Atomically record the identifier with the effect to prevent races.')
